<%- include('partials/header', { title }) %>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Why We Built It</p>
    <h1>Why This Lost and Found Platform Exists</h1>
    <p>Students lose important items all the time, and most of the time there is no single place to check. This platform solves that problem.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="stat-cluster">
    <article class="stat-card">
      <p>Registered Users</p>
      <strong><%= stats.total_users || 0 %></strong>
    </article>
    <article class="stat-card">
      <p>Open Cases</p>
      <strong><%= stats.open_listings || 0 %></strong>
    </article>
    <article class="stat-card">
      <p>Resolved Cases</p>
      <strong><%= stats.resolved_listings || 0 %></strong>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel prose-block">
  <h2 class="section-title">Problem We Are Solving</h2>
  <p>Students lose wallets, ID cards, chargers, notes, and keys. Recovery usually depends on random class groups and luck.</p>
  <p>We built one common platform so students know exactly where to post and where to search first.</p>
</section>

<section class="panel impact-strip">
  <article>
    <h3>Why this website was created</h3>
    <p>In college, lost items are common and communication is scattered. This website gives one trusted place for lost and found updates.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>How it helps daily student life</h3>
    <p>Students can post quickly, claim responsibly, and contact the owner directly without confusion.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>Trust and accountability</h3>
    <p>User accounts, login logs, and item status flow improve trust and make this practical for real use.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>For students</h3>
    <p>Fast listing, easy browse, and verified claim process reduce uncertainty and save time.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>For campus operations</h3>
    <p>A consistent digital record helps coordinate returns and improves transparency for administrators.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>For everyday use</h3>
    <p>Designed for around 10 to 50 daily users with clear screens and mobile-friendly pages.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="panel process-grid">
  <h2 class="section-title">Real-World Readiness Checklist</h2>
  <article class="step-card">
    <span>01</span>
    <h3>Role-based access</h3>
    <p>Only admin can open login audit pages and view platform-wide user activity.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="step-card">
    <span>02</span>
    <h3>Account recovery</h3>
    <p>Forgot Password flow with reset code support helps students recover access quickly.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="step-card">
    <span>03</span>
    <h3>Operational clarity</h3>
    <p>Open, claimed, and resolved statuses keep lifecycle tracking clean and transparent.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="panel process-grid">
  <h2 class="section-title">Platform Values</h2>
  <article class="step-card">
    <span>A</span>
    <h3>Accessibility</h3>
    <p>Simple UX for all students, even first-time users.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="step-card">
    <span>T</span>
    <h3>Trust</h3>
    <p>Authenticated accounts and admin-only audit visibility.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="step-card">
    <span>I</span>
    <h3>Impact</h3>
    <p>More recovered items, less stress, stronger campus community.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
